<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Samo's Empire</h1><p class="st-meta">623 CE – 658 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The first known Slavic political union, led by the Frankish merchant Samo, which threw off Avar rule and defeated a Frankish king.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Around 623 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavs">Slavs</a> of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, called <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wends">Wends</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chronicle-of-fredegar">Chronicle of Fredegar</a>, rebelled against their <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avars">Avar</a> overlords. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samo">Samo</a>, a Frankish merchant trading with them, fought so well that they chose him as king. The location of his realm is debated, but it probably covered <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-bohemia">Bohemia</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/great-moravia">Moravia</a>, parts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovakia">Slovakia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-austria">Lower Austria</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chronicle-of-fredegar">Fredegar</a>, the only substantial source, reports that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samo">Samo</a> ruled for 35 years, had twelve Slavic wives and won every battle against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avars">Avars</a>. In 631 a dispute over murdered Frankish merchants led <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dagobert-i">King Dagobert I</a> to invade; Samo defeated the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/franks">Franks</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-wogastisburg">Wogastisburg</a>, and the Sorb prince Dervan then joined him.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samo">Samo's</a> death around 658 his union seems to have dissolved, and nothing more is heard of it; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avars">Avars</a> regained influence in the region. It is remembered as a forerunner of later Slavic states such as <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/great-moravia">Great Moravia</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/carantania">Carantania</a>, though no direct continuity is known.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/samos-empire.jpg" alt="Samo's Empire" width="320" height="237"><figcaption>Image: Palickap · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:N%C3%A1klo_(vrch),_S%C3%A1mo_(2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>623 CE – 658 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Samo</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Slavic paganism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Common Slavic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/czech-republic">Czech Republic</a>, <a href="/countries/slovakia">Slovakia</a>, <a href="/countries/austria">Austria</a>, <a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Samo's realm, Realm of Samo</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=640&amp;focus=samos-empire" aria-label="Samo's Empire on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5038 449 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Samo's Empire lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5358 705h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5358 705h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Czech Republic. <a href="/atlas?year=640&amp;focus=samos-empire">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
